msgstr ""
"| Composerリファレンス                                 | QASMリファレンス |\n"
"| -------------------------------------------------- | -------------- |\n"
"| ![Identity gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/f3c1f16a-d5b4-4f1c-9f18-2d9b6dcfd2fe.avif) | `id q[0];`     |\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Phase gates {#phase-gates}"
msgstr "位相ゲート {#phase-gates}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**T gate**\n"
msgstr "**Tゲート**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The T gate is equivalent to RZ for the angle $\\pi/4$. Fault-tolerant quantum computers will compile all quantum programs down to just the T gate and its inverse, as well as the Clifford gates.\n"
msgstr "Tゲートは、角度 $\\pi/4$ のRZと等価です。フォールトトレラント量子コンピュータは、すべての量子プログラムをTゲートとその逆演算、およびCliffordゲートのみにコンパイルします。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Composer reference                                | OpenQASM reference | Q-sphere | Note about q-sphere representations                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![t\\_gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/b5f1b90c-d3b7-4f60-82f9-259dc40cef5b.avif) | `t q[0];`          | ![image29](/docs/images/guides/composer/c43496bb-89ff-4518-9afb-d276e400b032.avif)                              | The q-sphere representation shows the state after the gate operates on the initial equal superposition state $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ where $n$ is the number of qubits needed to support the gate. |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Composerリファレンス                                | OpenQASMリファレンス | Q-sphere | q-sphere表現に関する注意                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![t\\_gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/b5f1b90c-d3b7-4f60-82f9-259dc40cef5b.avif) | `t q[0];`          | ![image29](/docs/images/guides/composer/c43496bb-89ff-4518-9afb-d276e400b032.avif)                              | q-sphere表現は、ゲートが初期等重ね合わせ状態 $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $（$n$ はゲートをサポートするために必要なQubitの数）に作用した後の状態を示しています。 |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**S gate**\n"
msgstr "**Sゲート**\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The S gate applies a phase of $i$ to the $\\left|1\\right\\rangle$ state. It is equivalent to RZ for the angle $\\pi/2$. Note that S=P($\\pi/2$).\n"
msgstr "Sゲートは、$\\left|1\\right\\rangle$ 状態に位相 $i$ を適用します。角度 $\\pi/2$ のRZと等価です。なお、S=P($\\pi/2$) です。\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Composer reference                                | OpenQASM reference | Q-sphere | Note about q-sphere representations                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n"
"| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| ![s\\_gate](/docs/images/guides/composer/c3217084-41c0-4821-80fc-b0852a8c2cd4.avif) | `s q[0];`          | ![image25](/docs/images/guides/composer/ce2da6b1-c21b-4ec0-be82-984a874f02af.avif)                              | The q-sphere representation shows the state after the gate operates on the initial equal superposition state $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2^{n}}}\\sum_{i=0}^{2^{n}-1}\\vert i\\rangle, $ where $n$ is the number of qubits needed to support the gate. |\n"
msgstr ""
